From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 10:40:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): a mouse drag must not show the selection
 markers

Found by hand, one commit after it was introduced: a rightward drag on a
ghostty pane left a white sliver in the top-left corner of the pane.

It was not a rendering artifact. The selection markers are Windows Terminal's
touch-drag handles - XAML drawn over the swapchain, which is why nothing the
harness captures could ever contain them. Cascadia raises UpdateSelectionMarkers
on every selection change but with ClearMarkers *true* unless the selection is
a keyboard or mark-mode one, so a mouse drag hides them. The raise added for
copy-on-select passed false, which means show them - and TermControl places them
from SelectionInfo(), which this engine cannot fill in, so both handles landed
at cell (0,0).

False looks like the obviously-correct value there; the comment now says why it
is not.

Nothing automated could have caught this. Every selection check measures what
ghostty selected - text and cell spans - and none of them look at the pixels WT
draws on top of the pane. Recorded as a coverage gap rather than papered over.

WT suites: terminalCore 54/54, unitSettingsModel 159/159, unitControl 60/60,
terminalApp 51/51.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
---
 src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
index 833f2e6a8..93932f33e 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
@@ -946,7 +946,15 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         // A drag is about to make a selection, and ControlInteractivity decides
         // whether to copy it on release from this event - the click that began
         // the drag had nothing to copy yet and said so.
-        UpdateSelectionMarkers.raise(*this, winrt::make<implementation::UpdateSelectionMarkersEventArgs>(false));
+        //
+        // ClearMarkers is *true*, as it is on cascadia for a mouse drag: the
+        // markers are the keyboard/mark-mode affordance, and ControlCore only
+        // asks for them when SelectionMode() >= Keyboard. Passing false instead
+        // told TermControl to show them, and it places them from SelectionInfo(),
+        // which this engine cannot fill in - so both handles were drawn at cell
+        // (0,0) and a stray sliver appeared at the top-left of the pane on every
+        // rightward drag.
+        UpdateSelectionMarkers.raise(*this, winrt::make<implementation::UpdateSelectionMarkersEventArgs>(true));
     }
 
     void GhosttyControlCore::SetEndSelectionPoint(const Core::Point positionCore)
